            <div xml:id="d359">

                <pb facs="0694" n="558" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg558"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Pan American Airways, Inc./419:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Culbertson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-16T11:00:00-05:00">May 16, 1929—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>80. Chilean Post Office authorities have stated to representative of Pan
                    American-Grace Airways that cable from the United States Post Office to Chilean
                    postal authorities is regarded merely as information and that they desire to
                    negotiate directly with him with respect to rates to be paid by the Chilean
                    Government for the carriage of mails north. I have had no part in discussion but
                    would appreciate instructions as to how the United States Post Office desires
                    situation to be handled.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
